WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.038 --> 00:00:04.557
The ghost lifted its arm once again.

2
00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:11.338
Scrooge saw that they were back in the churchyard where Tiny Tim's funeral had taken place.

3
00:00:11.339 --> 00:00:17.335
Snow lay on the ground as before, but there was no clear, bright sky.

4
00:00:17.336 --> 00:00:22.816
Instead gray clouds dimmed the weak rays of the sun.

5
00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:30.496
The same priest stood in front of a different grave, looking down at a plain wooden coffin.

6
00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:34.396
This time no mourners were looking on.

7
00:00:34.397 --> 00:00:40.298
Only a couple of large men, gravediggers with spades, stood nearby.

8
00:00:40.299 --> 00:00:47.829
A cruel, cold wind howled, making the bare tree branches shudder and creak.

9
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:53.533
The priest shivered too, pulling his robe closer for warmth.

10
00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:58.443
A moment later he took out his pocket watch and checked the time.

11
00:00:58.444 --> 00:01:01.181
He nodded at the gravediggers.

12
00:01:01.182 --> 00:01:08.295
"Nobody is coming to this poor soul's burial. Go ahead and fill in the grave."

13
00:01:08.296 --> 00:01:13.702
As the priest hurried back into the church, the men set to work.

14
00:01:13.703 --> 00:01:20.300
They filled in the hole as quickly as they could.

15
00:01:20.301 --> 00:01:26.038
Then one jammed a square stone into place at the head of the grave.

16
00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:29.024
Scrooge stepped forward to see it.

17
00:01:29.025 --> 00:01:36.311
But he already knew what name he would see carved into the tombstone: Ebenezer Scrooge.

18
00:01:36.312 --> 00:01:41.020
"Nobody came to my funeral," he whispered.

19
00:01:41.021 --> 00:01:46.154
"Not Fred and his family, nor any of my business acquaintances.

20
00:01:46.155 --> 00:01:50.743
Even the priest didn't stay for the whole thing."

21
00:01:50.744 --> 00:01:56.997
The spirit lifted its arm, and for a moment, Scrooge was in a different place.

22
00:01:56.998 --> 00:02:00.104
It was a bedroom in Fred's house.

23
00:02:00.105 --> 00:02:05.577
Fred's youngest daughter was lying there, pale and ill.

24
00:02:05.578 --> 00:02:08.744
Fred's wife was kneeling beside her.

25
00:02:08.745 --> 00:02:16.719
Then Fred himself hurried in with a damp cloth, which he used to tenderly wipe the girl's face.

26
00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.109
"It's nearly time for your uncle's funeral," Fred's wife said.

27
00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.575
"You said you wanted to go."

28
00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:28.715
"I did." Fred adjusted his daughter's blankets.

29
00:02:28.716 --> 00:02:33.069
"But that was before our girl became ill."

30
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:37.405
"She's getting better, and the church isn't far," his wife said.

31
00:02:37.406 --> 00:02:41.553
"It wouldn't take you very long to pay your respects."

32
00:02:41.554 --> 00:02:46.832
"Yes, Papa," the young girl herself said, her voice rough with illness.

33
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:51.139
"I'm all right. Please go."

34
00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:56.259
Fred shrugged. "I haven't spoken to Uncle Scrooge in months.

35
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.099
He didn't seek my company when he was alive.

36
00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.479
So, I don't expect he'll miss me now that he's dead."

37
00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:11.477
Scrooge swallowed hard. "I see," he thought. "I see."

38
00:03:11.478 --> 00:03:18.035
With that, Fred's house disappeared, and the phantom pointed its finger upward at the sky.

39
00:03:18.036 --> 00:03:26.379
Scrooge looked up and watched the sun sink rapidly toward the horizon, moving as quickly as a racing horse.

40
00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.907
Just as quickly, it rose in the east.

41
00:03:29.908 --> 00:03:34.692
It flew across the sky, and then set again.

42
00:03:34.693 --> 00:03:40.687
It rose and set, over and over, moving faster and faster.

43
00:03:40.688 --> 00:03:45.385
Days, weeks, and months passed in a matter of minutes.

44
00:03:45.386 --> 00:03:51.923
Finally the ghost turned its finger once again in the direction of Scrooge's lonely grave.

45
00:03:51.924 --> 00:03:55.750
The grave looked even lonelier now.

46
00:03:55.751 --> 00:04:01.159
It was late summer, and grass had grown in over the bare earth.

47
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:09.435
Then weeds had sprouted, twisting vines and brambles, grabbing at the headstone and hiding the name on it.

48
00:04:09.436 --> 00:04:16.276
Someone had discarded a rusty tin can there, along with several scraps of newspaper.

49
00:04:16.277 --> 00:04:25.893
While nearby graves had flowers or mementos laid upon them, nobody had left anything to honor Ebenezer Scrooge.

50
00:04:25.894 --> 00:04:31.591
Scrooge stared at the headstone, his face pale and thoughtful.

51
00:04:31.592 --> 00:04:35.143
"Answer me one question, spirit.

52
00:04:35.144 --> 00:04:42.630
Are these the shadows of things that will happen, or are they just shadows of things that may happen?"

53
00:04:42.631 --> 00:04:49.224
The phantom didn't answer. It only continued pointing at the grave.

54
00:04:49.225 --> 00:04:54.978
"But, spirit, I'm not the man I was!" Scrooge cried.

55
00:04:54.979 --> 00:04:58.967
"I won't be the same man after what I've seen tonight.

56
00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:04.328
Why would you show me this terrible scene if I'm past all hope?"

57
00:05:04.329 --> 00:05:10.672
The spirit pointed from the grave to Scrooge, and then back again.

58
00:05:10.673 --> 00:05:13.392
Scrooge fell onto the ground.

59
00:05:13.393 --> 00:05:22.456
"Good spirit. Please tell me that it's still possible to change my future by changing my life in the present.

60
00:05:22.457 --> 00:05:26.605
That is all I want to know."

61
00:05:26.606 --> 00:05:30.237
The pointing hand trembled.

62
00:05:30.238 --> 00:05:35.502
"I promise to honor Christmas in my heart," Scrooge said.

63
00:05:35.503 --> 00:05:40.380
"I'll try to remember its lessons all year long.

64
00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:46.514
Please tell me there is time, and I can still make things better!"

65
00:05:46.515 --> 00:05:50.818
In desperation, Scrooge grabbed the spirit's hand.

66
00:05:50.819 --> 00:05:54.011
The Ghost of Christmas Future yanked free.

67
00:05:54.012 --> 00:06:03.898
A moment later the ghost shrunk and collapsed until it was nothing but a wooden bedpost.

